Z||000026||Cheever2||09-10-2000||05:05 PM||||Hello Babygirl, and all others...<P>I'm new here also.  When my Grand Am died last year I went shopping and found a perfect black '88 Fiero GT and HAD to have it.  Two months later I lost control in a heavy rain and tried to go into the Astrodome without tickets.  Insurance co. wouldn't fix it but I kept it anyway and got another '88.  This one's a 4-cyl. coupe but pretty nice.  Does anybody else have trouble keeping it in a straight line in the rain?  I'm 43 and am a very good driver (I know everybody says that), but Fieros don't handle like anything else I've driven... must be the mid-engine weight distribution.  Anyway that's another topic, but I absolutely love these cars, and have quickly become a fanatic.  Hoping to turn the GT into a Fino someday.  Enough for now.  ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Patrick||09-10-2000||08:10 PM||||<BR>Welcome <B>Cheever</B>. Just so there's no perceived favoritism with new forum members, I felt I should speak up <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Regarding the handling of Fieros on wet roads, I live in the rain forest here on the west coast and I've never had a problem.<P>Hmmmm... Strange we haven't had any clarification yet on who/what <B>Babygirl</B> is. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  <BR>||||reg||14
